From 58b9885996ff3b18f168b2d336018a11b5f7474b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:35:43 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] kcm_bluetooth: Device page with sections on the device
 sub-page, no false "no adapter" while starting
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Device (docs/page-design.md section 1): paired-device list on the main page, each device opens its own Form
sub-page (kcm.push("Device.qml")), adapter/login/file settings on a second sub-page. That structure already existed
and stays. BluezQt calls, GlobalSettings/FileReceiverSettings keys, wizard launch, NAP/DUN setup and Forget dialog are
unchanged; main_mediacenter.qml and DeviceConnectionSidebar.qml untouched.

Moved / renamed:
- Device sub-page order by use: Connect/Disconnect and Name first, then "Connection" (Trusted, Blocked + help),
  "Sharing" (Send File…, Setup NAP/DUN Network…; the section title shows only while one of these buttons does),
  "Details" (Type, Battery, Address, Adapter), and "Forget Device…" last. Trusted/Blocked: Switch -> CheckBox (a
  Form uses checkboxes, section 3). "Send File" -> "Send File…", "Forget" -> "Forget Device…" (they open something).
  Rows root-device-connected/name/trusted/blocked, Send-File, Setup-NAP/DUN-Network, Forget, DeviceType/Battery/
  Address/Adapter.
- Settings sub-page: toolbar action "Configure…" -> "Settings…" (ConfigureSettings). Adapter Enabled/Visible
  switches -> checkboxes "Adapter: Enabled" and "Visible to other devices" (Enabled, Visible); sections "Login"
  (On login radios) and "Received Files" got titles; the folder row is a RowLayout and its icon-only button has a
  tooltip and accessible name (Select-folder).
- Main page: list rows now say "Connected" / "Blocked" first in the subtitle (model-Name); the empty state "No devices
  paired" carries the action "Pair Device…" (NoDevices, PairDevice).
- Relabel table: inventory/relabel/kcm_bluetooth.tsv (outer repo). Inventory --strict: 34 rows ok, 0 lost.

Speed: the first frame waits on the BluezQt manager (async init job, bluetooth.cpp; nothing synchronous in the KCM).
The page now shows at once and a BusyIndicator appears only if the manager is still not operational after 150 ms.
"No Bluetooth adapters found" was shown whenever rfkill.state was Unknown, which is also the state before the manager
is operational; it now needs Manager.operational too, so it no longer flashes at startup (assumption, see below).
After-numbers: pending, manager will measure.

HIG: HIG-001/005/006, HIG-057. Not built yet. Not confirmed without BluezQt headers (not in src/master): that
rfkill.state is Unknown before Manager.operational (the message condition is safe either way: it only gets stricter),
and that Device.connected/blocked are readable from the list-row helper infoText (same properties Device.qml
already uses).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
